version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/creelie/eCon/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/eCon"
abstract: >-
  LaTeX source, figures and the exact-arithmetic check program of the paper
  "Subexponential Weighted Counting and Exact Optimisation", which deduces
  from the summation routine of OpenAI's preprint "The Exponential Time
  Hypothesis is False" (25 October 2026), reproduced in full with credit,
  deterministic 2^{o(n)} algorithms for weighted counting and exact
  optimisation on sparse constraint systems: Max-k-SAT profiles, Max-Cut and
  bisections, the independence polynomial of every graph, Vertex Cover in
  2^{o(k)} + poly(n), partition functions on bounded-degree graphs, Ising and
  Potts densities of states, sparse permanents, and SNP contained in SE.
